      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Mount Utsayantha rises 3,214 feet inside Stamford and hosts an observatory and viewing tower for stargazers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stamford%2C_New_York",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The mountain and nearby lake were named after Utsayantha, an Indian princess whose story the village preserves.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2,
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://villageofstamfordny.gov/about-us/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The West Branch Delaware River forms Stamford’s northern border and flows through its upper reaches.",
